  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Not sure if this is an issue exclusive to this Open Beta but we have discovered that if you do an animation on an avatar and interrupt it before it finishes by switching into another avatar, your tracking is not restored and your avatar is either in a generic state or your lose access to hand gestures. Also tested, Reset Avatar does not fix the issue.\nThis works for both AV2 models and AV3 models and switching from AV2 to AV2, AV2 to AV3, AV3 to AV2 and AV3 to AV3. \nI have a YouTube video that goes through three examples of this here: https://youtu.be/yPNe3FqXTfM\nSteps to reproduce: \n1. With the expression menu, start an animation.\n2. Close the expression menu without canceling the animation.\n3. Change into another avatar.\n4. Experience results. \nI imagine this problem has to do with the fact that by interrupting the animation the avatar does not go into a RestoreTracking state to restore tracking. It is strange that the problem persists between avatars.\n\nEdit, an additional note that I recently remembered! If you're doing an animation that you can move in, for example: one that doesn't automatically cancel when you move, and you fall off the map and hit the respawn border, your tracking in that case also tends to get messed up and odd too. I've experienced this on a previous build with some friends",
